# Byproduct of `./gradlew :app:dependencies --write-locks`, which regenerates
# android/app/gradle.lockfile (that one IS committed and IS scanned). This file
# only ever locks the settings-level version-catalog classpath and resolves to
# `empty=incomingCatalogForLibs0`, so it carries no dependency information to
# scan and OSV-Scanner has no parser for the filename. Ignored so regenerating
# the runtime lock does not leave an unclassifiable manifest in the tree.
android/settings-gradle.lockfile
